    "proof": "The summable drift bound makes every fixed core Cauchy in the finite-dimensional operator norm, and summing the tail gives the quantitative error estimate. Leading-core restriction commutes with the limit, so Q_(m+1) restricts to Q_m. Interlacing gives lambda_min(A_N^[m])>=lambda_min(A_N)>=-eta_N; norm convergence and eta_N->0 therefore make Q_m positive semidefinite. Every vector in c_00 lies in one such core. For the no-go statement take the one-dimensional core A_N=H_N. Its adjacent drift 1/(N+1) tends to zero, but the harmonic sequence diverges.",
